;; Regulatory source register for JPN-MOFA ODA / JICA tender-eligibility compliance.
;;
;; README.md says: "Every regulatory claim must cite the official MOFA source."
;; Until this file existed there was no such list, so no claim in this
;; repository could be traced to anything. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. Follows the catalog convention of
;; cloud-itonami-iso3166-jpn's src/statute/facts.cljc: a law not in this table
;; has NO spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an
;; id or a URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljs`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it. The two
;; checks are not interchangeable, and the reason is the main thing this file
;; has to teach:
;;
;;   :http-2xx      Fetch and require 2xx. Sound for www.mofa.go.jp and
;;                  www.jica.go.jp, which were measured 2026-08-26 to answer a
;;                  real 404 for a missing page.
;;
;;   :e-gov-law-id  Resolve the law id through the e-Gov law API and require the
;;                  title and law number to still match what is written below.
;;                  HTTP status is NOT consulted for these and must not be:
;;                  laws.e-gov.go.jp is a single-page app that answers
;;                  **HTTP 200 for /law/<anything>**, including ids that do not
;;                  exist, and renders "not found" client-side. Measured
;;                  2026-08-26: the invented id 999ZZ9999999999 returns 200 --
;;                  and so did 322CO0000000165, which is what this register
;;                  first wrote for 予算決算及び会計令 before the API answered
;;                  total_count 0. The correct id is 322IO0000000165; 勅令 is
;;                  IO, not CO. A 200 from this host is not evidence of
;;                  anything, and the verifier proves its own e-Gov branch can
;;                  still tell the difference before it reports a pass.
;;
;; MEASURING THE SOURCE IS NOT THE SAME AS MEASURING THE PROBE. An earlier
;; draft of this file recorded every www.mofa.go.jp entry as unreachable, with
;; a measured 403 from four curl invocations and one independent egress. That
;; was wrong: MOFA answers 200 with full content to Node's fetch, with or
;; without a User-Agent, at the same moment curl gets 403 over both HTTP/2 and
;; HTTP/1.1. The block is on the TLS fingerprint, not on the request -- so the
;; refusal belonged to the tool, and a curl-based verifier would have written a
;; permanent false "this authority cannot be checked" into the register while
;; looking like it had measured something. scripts/verify-facts.cljs uses fetch.
;;
;; :source/covers says why an entry is in a MOFA-ODA-tender register. Claims
;; stop at the level actually checked -- law identity, and for the agency pages
;; the title and headings read on 2026-08-26. No article text is asserted,
;; because no article text was read.

